## Context

Ticket 0270 parent tracker (implemented by child 0276 after 0274/0275) produces
`sota_cross_eval.csv` with 12 mechanical scores per run.
This ticket renders those scores as a radar/spider chart — one polygon per model
or arm — so quality profiles are visually comparable across experiments and modelsets.

The modelset to display should be driven by a YAML config file (analogous to how
`experiments/figures.toml` or the model registry drives other figures), not hardcoded.

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/plot_quality_spider.py` — new script (primary deliverable)
- `experiments/figures.toml` or new `experiments/prompts/quality_spider.yaml` — modelset config
- `report/inputs/generated/fig_quality_spider.pdf` — output artifact
- `Makefile` — add target wiring `sota_cross_eval.csv` → `fig_quality_spider.pdf`

## Actions

1. Create a YAML config file (e.g. `experiments/quality_spider_config.yaml`) with:
   - `modelset`: list of model IDs to include
   - `axes`: ordered list of axis names to display (default: all 5)
   - `arms`: which arms to overlay (e.g. `[naive, optimised]`)
   - `aggregate`: how to aggregate reps (`median` default)

2. Implement `src/aedist/plot_quality_spider.py`:
   - Reads `sota_cross_eval.csv` and the YAML config
   - Computes per-model/arm median score per axis (normalised to [0, 1] for display)
   - Renders a matplotlib polar plot with one polygon per model/arm
   - Writes PDF to `report/inputs/generated/fig_quality_spider.pdf`
   - Uses the project's existing color palette / style conventions (check `plot_*.py`)

3. Wire in `Makefile`:
   ```makefile
   fig_quality_spider.pdf: sota_cross_eval.csv quality_spider_config.yaml
       uv run python -m aedist.plot_quality_spider ...
   ```

4. Add `\includegraphics{fig_quality_spider}` placeholder in report where appropriate.

## Normalisation note

Different axes have different natural maxima:
- Accuracy: F1 ∈ [0, 1] — use directly
- Coherence/Provenance/Temporality/FC: fractions ∈ [0, 1] — use directly
- The five axes are already on the same [0, 1] scale. No rescaling needed.

## Test

- Canned 3-row `sota_cross_eval.csv` → PDF written without error
- Config with 2 models, 2 arms → 4 polygons in the output
- Config with unknown model ID → logged warning, silently skipped (not crash)

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `plot_quality_spider.py` exists with YAML-driven modelset config
- [ ] `fig_quality_spider.pdf` generated from current `sota_cross_eval.csv`
- [ ] Makefile target present and wired
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
